# Test-only environment overrides for pytest.
#
# Loaded by tests/conftest.py (with override=True) before any test
# module imports `main` or `users.config` - so these values win over
# whatever backend/.env (the real local/production env file, gitignored,
# holds actual secrets) sets for the same keys. Everything else - DB/
# Redis connection settings, USERS_JWT_SECRET, GROQ_API_KEY, ... - still
# comes from backend/.env as before, unchanged; this file only overrides
# the couple of keys that make pytest behave like a non-production run
# instead of silently inheriting backend/.env's production configuration.
#
# Safe to commit: no secrets here.

# TrustedHostMiddleware is opt-in - main.py only adds it when this is
# non-empty (see main.py's "SERVER STEP 5" comment). Left unset here so
# TestClient's default `Host: testserver` header isn't rejected with a
# 400 "Invalid host header", which otherwise cascades into failures
# across nearly every /auth, /portfolios, /dashboard, /paper-trading,
# /watchlists and /quant endpoint test.
ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# Keeps _validate_production_config() and any other ENVIRONMENT ==
# "production" branch (see tests/test_main_production_hardening.py)
# from firing during a local test run just because backend/.env is
# configured for the deployed container.
ENVIRONMENT=
